# connections.svg is NOT regenerated automatically: fdp's output is not stable
# across graphviz versions. The committed SVG came from graphviz 2.43.0; running
# the script under 15.1.0 relays the whole graph and rewrites ~250 lines for the
# same diagram, so any machine with a different graphviz churns the file.
# Consecutive runs on one machine do agree — this is version drift, not randomness
# in the force-directed layout.
#
# The committed connections.svg is therefore the artifact of record. Regenerate it
# deliberately if src/rice_connections.dot changes:
#
#     cd content/posts/smart-rice-cooker/media && ./src/rice_build.sh
#
# and expect a large positional diff whenever your graphviz differs from the one
# that produced the current file.
PROCESS_SCRIPT=false
